{"posts":[{"id":"flaglimits_p27_651","t":"In these I tried to find some down moves as well to train eye for some reason I see QM's at tops easier than bottoms.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#651","p":27,"im":["b10332d3b55718817a055ec4a20aec1946b1a024","8ac18ec078e03771789d937895b3a7fa5bdc3bc3","a9810d89d31e869c7aa693559c6c64fc7e89fc4d","c5a9404795647dc0215bc42516574904972339a6"],"m":651},{"id":"flaglimits_p27_652","t":"Here we go...i read all the thread and i start doing my HW","a":"—","d":"","n":"#652","p":27,"im":[],"m":652},{"id":"flaglimits_p27_654","t":"I have been spending the last few days trying to come to terms with Flag Limits, I hope I am heading in the right direction. The below chart is one that I found a little more tricky; deducing the boundaries for the flag limit is something I really need to work on. I'm finding that sometimes there is more than one way to define the boundaries which then cause confusion as to whether a candle enters the flag or not for a FTB.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#654","p":27,"im":["63dc518b400fd24839070ae730409457f7395fe8"],"m":654},{"id":"flaglimits_p27_655","t":"Here's how I'd mark the FL's","a":"—","d":"","n":"#655","p":27,"im":[],"m":655},{"id":"flaglimits_p27_656","t":"Thanks for the feedback Redbullish, much appreciated!:)","a":"—","d":"","n":"#656","p":27,"im":[],"m":656},{"id":"flaglimits_p27_657","t":"Take what I said with a grain of salt, i'm a newbie here","a":"—","d":"","n":"#657","p":27,"im":[],"m":657},{"id":"flaglimits_p27_658","t":"dcabfx\n\nRedbullish, your marking is very good and I like that you're watching for the return and the engulf. Very nice, keep it up. A suggestion if I may is to look out for flags, mark the limit, watch them respected, then broken and watch for what price does when returning to that area again. Track and mark that too (the breaks) and you'll see something that really lights you up. Do this starting from as far back as you can go and with any instrument. FL's are amazing and the opportunities when price returns and the engulfs of them will pave the road for great things.\n\nEnjoy! dcabfx","a":"—","d":"","n":"#658","p":27,"im":[],"m":658},{"id":"flaglimits_p27_659","t":"Hi dcabfx, are u look out base of pole too? Sometimes imo FL more important than base of pole, am i right?\n\nthanks","a":"—","d":"","n":"#659","p":27,"im":[],"m":659},{"id":"flaglimits_p27_660","t":"dcabfx\n\nThat's a great question and I'm noticing it's your first post. Welcome!! The base of the pole is important as well. It's what makes up the Bull or Bear flag as a whole so it needs attention also.\n\nI'm not sure where you are in terms of technical analysis or even the markets but I would encourage you to go through Markeopedia and get up to speed on things over there and start with some Supply and Demand pockets (CAPS).\n\ndcabfx","a":"—","d":"","n":"#660","p":27,"im":[],"m":660},{"id":"flaglimits_p27_661","t":"dcabfx wrote: Redbullish, your marking is very good and I like that you're watching for the return and the engulf. Very nice, keep it up. A suggestion if I may is to look out for flags, mark the limit, watch them respected, then broken and watch for what price does when returning to that area again. Track and mark that too (the breaks) and you'll see something that really lights you up. Do this starting from as far back as you can go and with any instrument. FL's are amazing and the opportunities when price returns and the engulfs of them will pave the road for great things.\n\nThank you for your feedback dcab, very appreciated. For now, i'm mainly focusing on correctly mark the FLs. I noticed that sometimes the price react to the H / L level, other times to the O/C level. The example above on EURGBP is very clear, and it is the rule that i use currently, but i don't know if it's right!\n\n....and sometimes, neither works:\n\nWhat do you think about the GBPNZD?","a":"—","d":"","n":"#661","p":27,"im":[],"m":661},{"id":"flaglimits_p27_662","t":"Hi Everybody, I guess right they sai